        "original_id": "4b6f62f6-4994-56ea-bf5b-18925f738550",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Massachusetts's 11th congressional district\n- People: Brian Donnelly, John Quincy Adams, John F. Kennedy, Tip O'Neill\n- Roles: Congressman, President of the United States, Speaker, diplomat, United States Senator, member of the House of Representatives\n\nFacts:\n- John Quincy Adams was born on July 11, 1767, and died on February 23, 1848.\n- John Quincy Adams was an American statesman who served as a diplomat, a United States Senator, a member of the House of Representatives, and the sixth President of the United States from 1825 to 1829.\n- John Quincy Adams was a notable Congressman from Massachusetts's 11th congressional district after serving as president.\n- John F. Kennedy was a notable Congressman from Massachusetts's 11th congressional district before he became president.\n- Tip O'Neill was a notable Congressman from Massachusetts's 11th congressional district and later became Speaker.\n- Brian Donnelly was the last Congressman of Massachusetts's 11th congressional district.",
